From d88807a4d0e681cf054dace24dee4415d54e7ca4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:09:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] F-5: the Follow camera's step over his head eases instead
 of jumping

- CAM-OVERSIGHT (camera.js _chase): whether the view on the way over his head still sees him is asked
  of his head or chest, as before CAM-ROOFEDGE; with the legs rule asked there too the step was taken
  whenever a roof's edge hid his legs (2.1-3.4 m in a frame on the street, the door and the house-door
  routes: all of v75's new kept-out-of-a-wall jumps). The legs rule still chooses the view (armFor).
- And the step goes at most CH_OVER_SEE_STEP (0.9 m) a frame, through clear spots.
- why.keepBy names which keep-out rule moved the camera (tests/lib/camrec.js traces it).
- CAM-COVER: the crowns marked sight.soft count once he has stood CH_SOFT_T s (world.js, next commit).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
